natives": ["B1", "B3", "B4"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=100%, source=both]\n\nMechanical Bowel Obstruction vs Functional Gastrointestinal Disorder:\n  Favours first:  abdominal bloating, abdominal cramping, abdominal pain, blood in stool, dark-colored urine\n  Favours second: cognitive impairment, gait disturbance, nonepileptic seizures, pain, paralysis\n\nMechanical Bowel Obstruction vs Biliary Tract Disease:\n  Favours first:  abdominal bloating, abdominal cramping, abdominal pain, blood in stool, diarrhea\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n\nMechanical Bowel Obstruction vs Pancreatic Insufficiency:\n  Favours first:  abdominal bloating, abdominal cramping, blood in stool, dark-colored urine, fever\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n\nMechanical Bowel Obstruction vs Infectious Gastroenteritis:\n  Favours first:  abdominal bloating, abdominal cramping, blood in stool, dark-colored urine, firm abdomen\n  Favours second: abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract, ascites, atopic dermatitis, bloody diarrhea, body aches\n\nFunctional Gastrointestinal Disorder vs Biliary Tract Disease:\n  Favours first:  cognitive impairment, nonepileptic seizures, pain, paralysis, sensory loss\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n\nFunctional Gastrointestinal Disorder vs Pancreatic Insufficiency:\n  Favours first:  cognitive impairment, nonepileptic seizures, pain, paralysis, sensory loss\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity\n\nFunctional Gastrointestinal Disorder 